<title>SOUTH KOREA: TABLE-HANJIN SHIPPING H1 NET SHRINKS.</title>
<headline>TABLE-HANJIN SHIPPING H1 NET SHRINKS.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)				   340    vs   782</p>
<p>    Net					     4.13 vs     9.11</p>
<p>    Turnover				  1,210.9  vs   950.83</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			   4.13  vs    9.11</p>
<p>Note - Hanjin Shipping Co Ltd, a unit of Hanjin Group HANJ.CN, is one of South Korea's leading shipping firms. Its earnings fell on foreign exchange losses and low freight rates, a company official said. Its share capital rose to 12.14 million shares by end-June from 11.76 million a year ago due to conversion of bonds to stocks.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
